WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
What's up y'all? This is Brad. I'm the founder and owner of Second Line

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.400
Clothing. I just want to get on here and introduce myself and explain what

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.400
Second Line is. Second Line is a Louisiana culture project that's built

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.740
around my passion for streetwear. A lot of clothing brands just put graphics on

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.400
shirts and sell them and that's not what this is. Every collection is going to focus on

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.600
a different city, town, neighborhood, community in Louisiana and the goal is

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.400
going to be document the places, document the people, document the stories,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.020
the things that locals actually remember not the tourist version of

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.360
Louisiana. This is the real Louisiana. This is going to be the corner stores, the

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:44.240
neighborhoods, the slang, the businesses that have been around, the landmarks, the

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.400
the memories, the things that make each place different. For every collection I'll

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.280
travel to that community. I'll talk to the people, visit local businesses, document

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.160
real locations and build a limited clothing collection inspired on what I

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.040
find. The first collection is going to be Baton Rouge because that's where I'm from.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:07.160
It's where I grew up. It's where I became who I am. After that we move on to

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.120
the next city and I'll just do that one collection at a time, one story at a time.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.560
But for now I do have some Louisiana culture shirts up on my site that you

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.960
can grab. Be on the lookout for the first Baton Rouge drop and let me know

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.840
which city I should do after that. Welcome to Second Line.
